{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The `upsert_command` command creates or updates a backend command definition within a specified library and control, validating its language, parameters, and return type before persisting the associated Rust code and imports. Upon successful storage, it automatically triggers a compilation process to verify the code's integrity and returns a status object indicating success or detailing any compilation errors. CONTRACT: `code_body` is the FUNCTION BODY ONLY — the system generates `pub fn <cmd>(<params>) -> <return_type>` around it. Never include a fn signature in code_body. Declared params are in scope as named variables of their Rust types. The final expression of code_body must be a value of the declared return_type. Put use statements in `imports`. Updating an existing command preserves its meta and impl records' readers/writers (its security gating); a new command starts admin-only until set_groups grants access. JAVASCRIPT/TYPESCRIPT (lang `javascript` or `typescript`): code_body is the body of a JavaScript function (async when it uses await) whose parameters are the declared params, in order; it ends with `return <value>`, not a final expression. A typescript body may carry type annotations. `imports` holds ES `import` lines for npm packages installed in node_modules next to data/, or for another JavaScript/TypeScript command as `flowlang:<lib>/<ctl>/<cmd>` (its function is the default export; what its imports field exports comes along) - bundled with esbuild; there is no require, process, Buffer or Node built-in. The compile step checks syntax (and bundles imports); run check_js afterwards for the type check. JOURNALED on the control's patch journal (facet \"command\", cmd = the name, op \"create\" or \"upsert\", old/new = the {command, impl} record data as JSON - the shape delete_command journals; old is empty on create), with compile ok|err, also when the compile fails, because the store has changed either way. An upsert that changes nothing writes no entry. The result carries patch_id when an entry was written, or journal_warning when the edit landed but could not be journaled. label is the stated reason for the edit, recorded on the entry (the why-harvest pairs it with the change; empty is allowed and records no reason); an empty author defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::unique_session_id::unique_session_id;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::data;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse crate::dev::dev::compile::compile;","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"name":"cmd","type":"String"},{"name":"lang","type":"String"},{"name":"return_type","type":"String"},{"name":"params","type":"JSONArray"},{"name":"imports","type":"String"},{"name":"code_body","type":"String"},{"desc":"The stated reason for this edit, recorded on the journal entry (the why-harvest pairs it with the change). May be empty, which records no reason.","name":"label","type":"String"},{"desc":"Who is making the edit, recorded on the journal entry. Empty defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous.","name":"author","type":"String"},{"desc":"Request metadata filled in by the framework; pass an empty string from tools.","name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"ovwolr19ec8c38800z1047","readers":[],"time":1794510456761,"username":"system","writers":[]}